WEBVTT

00:08.633 --> 00:12.053
MEOTO ZENZAI

00:19.686 --> 00:20.812
Dokuga.

00:20.895 --> 00:23.815
Tetsujo. How's Risu doing?

00:23.898 --> 00:25.817
Well, he's sleeping for now.

00:26.735 --> 00:27.819
I see.

00:30.238 --> 00:32.741
Dokuga. You know, don't you?

00:33.575 --> 00:35.577
You know who killed Risu?

00:36.327 --> 00:40.081
Yeah. I saw him die with my own two eyes.

00:41.082 --> 00:43.084
Then... who did it?

00:50.175 --> 00:53.553
This paper-airplane letter is from Kento.

02:22.016 --> 02:23.935
THE BEGINNING

02:26.771 --> 02:32.068
Boss, we made you your favorite.
Please enjoy it.

02:32.152 --> 02:36.156
I was able to obtain
some really wonderful parts today.

02:39.284 --> 02:43.830
The black powder has run out,
and our organization has weakened.

02:44.330 --> 02:47.292
But this time,
we can take advantage of this woman.

02:50.795 --> 02:53.214
That smells pretty good.

02:53.965 --> 02:55.592
It's ravioli!

02:56.593 --> 02:57.468
Damn it!

02:57.552 --> 02:59.220
What the hell is this?

03:02.974 --> 03:04.225
Whoa!

03:05.101 --> 03:05.977
Dammit.

03:06.060 --> 03:08.021
That was close.

03:08.938 --> 03:11.357
Bastard! Where did you get that mask?

03:12.817 --> 03:15.862
As you can see, it's your partner's mask.

03:15.945 --> 03:19.407
Taking you hostage
made it really easy to kill him.

03:19.949 --> 03:23.870
No way. Shin got killed?

03:30.627 --> 03:32.295
I'll kill you!

03:51.856 --> 03:52.815
Boss...

03:52.899 --> 03:53.816
What?

03:53.900 --> 03:56.069
Help me.

03:58.071 --> 04:00.698
I don't wanna die.

04:04.285 --> 04:06.663
Help...

04:14.462 --> 04:17.423
Noi's not here.

04:19.384 --> 04:20.426
Shin!

04:21.386 --> 04:23.763
Your body's so cold.

04:23.846 --> 04:26.641
We have to find Noi.

04:26.724 --> 04:28.643
You can't push yourself anymore!

04:31.104 --> 04:32.272
Shin!

04:36.109 --> 04:37.652
Noi! Are you all right?

05:15.815 --> 05:18.609
Too slow for me, you giant freak!

05:18.693 --> 05:21.738
Ouch, that hurts.

05:22.405 --> 05:24.240
Gigantification magic?

05:32.582 --> 05:33.583
Noi!

05:34.083 --> 05:36.502
Good. You're alive.

05:37.086 --> 05:41.507
Hey, what are you doing behind there?

05:44.969 --> 05:47.513
It's a wax figure.

05:53.186 --> 05:55.855
- Mr. Kasukabe! What are you doing?
- What?

05:55.938 --> 05:58.274
This house is going to collapse! Get out!

06:13.081 --> 06:19.003
Boss, come... back...

06:21.381 --> 06:22.632
Mr. Kasukabe.

06:25.426 --> 06:28.137
Mr. Kasukabe...

06:29.806 --> 06:32.141
Ouch.

06:36.062 --> 06:37.772
This figure's face

06:38.439 --> 06:40.775
looks just like him.

06:42.110 --> 06:44.862
But why...

06:50.660 --> 06:51.702
Hayes.

06:52.745 --> 06:53.913
Hayes.

06:53.996 --> 06:56.082
Wake up, Hayes.

06:56.165 --> 07:00.420
Who is it?
That name was lost to the past long ago.

07:01.003 --> 07:02.922
- Hayes.
- Haru?

07:03.005 --> 07:04.173
Hayes.

07:05.007 --> 07:07.093
It's been quite a while, Hayes.

07:07.176 --> 07:10.680
I didn't recognize you at first
because you look like this.

07:10.763 --> 07:13.391
It's been a while
since I woke up my husband.

07:13.474 --> 07:14.475
What?

07:15.726 --> 07:18.813
As I was flying,
I smelled something nostalgic.

07:19.355 --> 07:23.943
Looks like you're still
writing books under my name.

07:24.026 --> 07:25.987
Professor Kasukabe.

07:26.070 --> 07:27.947
Haru, you're...

07:28.030 --> 07:31.451
Yeah. I became a devil.

07:31.534 --> 07:36.330
I couldn't let go of my old dream,
so I took the devil exam.

07:37.123 --> 07:42.003
But I couldn't return to the Hole.
That was a horrible thing I did to you.

07:43.754 --> 07:47.300
It's okay. I'm just glad you're alive.

07:47.383 --> 07:49.594
Here, this is yours, I believe.

07:53.931 --> 07:56.100
Thank you, Hayes.

08:01.939 --> 08:05.109
Thank good... Whoa! It all burned down!

08:05.193 --> 08:07.111
No wonder it felt so hot.

08:07.195 --> 08:09.113
- Hey, guys!
- What?

08:09.197 --> 08:10.781
Are you both okay?

08:10.865 --> 08:12.325
- Doc?
- Doc?

08:13.242 --> 08:15.620
That's Shin and his partner.

08:15.703 --> 08:18.915
Wait, did they come to save us?

08:18.998 --> 08:22.084
They're fine.
Thankfully, they're both still alive.

08:22.168 --> 08:26.255
What a shame.
You never got to see your wife.

08:26.339 --> 08:29.425
Actually, I did see her.

08:39.352 --> 08:42.522
How long have you known about Nikaido?

08:51.113 --> 08:56.035
Why did you choose to hide
The Sorcerer Who Manipulates Time?

08:56.118 --> 08:58.871
Answer me, Asu.

09:07.046 --> 09:12.426
You, a natural-born devil,
could never understand, Chidaruma.

09:13.553 --> 09:14.679
Very well.

09:27.483 --> 09:31.821
Come on, what even is this place?
There's not a single person around.

09:31.904 --> 09:35.783
Throwing us into a place like this,
that damn pig-faced devil.

09:35.866 --> 09:40.246
Caiman, I think Asu
deliberately chose a deserted area.

09:40.329 --> 09:42.206
If En finds us, it'll be bad.

09:42.290 --> 09:44.834
Magic doesn't work on me, you know!

09:44.917 --> 09:46.919
I'm not afraid of En!

09:47.420 --> 09:53.843
Asu said if I meet En now,
I'll end up becoming his partner again.

09:55.553 --> 09:59.098
I don't want you as my enemy anymore.

09:59.181 --> 10:03.603
If that wasn't enough,
that heart-faced bastard is a pain too.

10:04.145 --> 10:06.647
Asu... I wonder if he's okay.

10:08.691 --> 10:09.900
Caiman.

10:09.984 --> 10:12.695
Ain't this a subway entrance?

10:14.614 --> 10:16.365
Mastema?

10:17.241 --> 10:22.622
This is the town where En fought
the Cross-Eyes boss six years ago.

10:27.918 --> 10:29.295
The Mastema Underground Mall!

10:32.423 --> 10:35.843
This place feels like the Hole.

10:35.926 --> 10:38.346
We might get some clothes and knives.

10:38.429 --> 10:41.766
But we don't have any money,
so we'll have to rob again.

10:41.849 --> 10:43.351
Or shoplift.

10:44.894 --> 10:46.062
- Caiman.
- What?

10:46.145 --> 10:49.565
Stay alert. There's someone tailing us.

10:49.649 --> 10:50.816
Really?

10:58.741 --> 10:59.825
What?

11:00.451 --> 11:01.786
Where are they?

11:04.413 --> 11:07.833
Who the hell are you?
Why were you following us?

11:07.917 --> 11:10.836
Wait! I'm one of you!

11:10.920 --> 11:12.797
One of us, you say?

11:12.880 --> 11:13.839
Caiman.

11:14.465 --> 11:15.758
Let her go.

11:17.009 --> 11:17.927
Ouch!

11:18.552 --> 11:21.055
So rough... It hurts!

11:21.138 --> 11:22.139
Who are you?

11:22.807 --> 11:25.226
It's just like yours, see?

11:25.309 --> 11:26.227
- What?
- What?

11:26.977 --> 11:29.730
I just got it on one eye last week.

11:33.150 --> 11:37.113
You guys are new in town, aren't you?
I've never seen you before.

11:37.196 --> 11:41.117
I work under Mr. Maki. My name is Natsuki.

11:41.200 --> 11:44.203
Well, you could say I'm a rookie dealer.

11:44.704 --> 11:47.540
- You guys came to see Mr. Maki, right?
- What?

11:47.623 --> 11:49.625
Just play along with her, Caiman.

11:49.709 --> 11:53.379
Yeah! That's right! How's Mr. Maki doing?

11:53.462 --> 11:57.383
Business hasn't been great lately,
so he's looking pretty worn out.

11:58.008 --> 12:01.345
Sorry, I've got to do my job,
so just wait a bit!

12:06.976 --> 12:09.603
What the hell is that girl selling?

12:09.687 --> 12:12.690
Thanks for waiting!
I'll call Mr. Maki now.

12:12.773 --> 12:16.277
But before that, Natsuki,
there's something I want to ask.

12:16.360 --> 12:17.194
PAWN SHOP

12:17.737 --> 12:20.781
Hey, old hag!
Sell them some weapons and clothes.

12:20.865 --> 12:24.535
- Wow!
- Whoa, this is awesome!

12:24.618 --> 12:30.166
Rumor has it, some of the stuff here was
sold by the Cross-Eyes boss and his aides.

12:30.249 --> 12:31.917
Really?

12:32.001 --> 12:35.880
Well, take your time picking.
I'm going to work.

12:37.673 --> 12:41.886
Come on! There's nothing
in this place that fits me, damn it!

12:41.969 --> 12:44.555
Caiman, I've made my choice!

12:46.891 --> 12:52.313
I'm not done yet!
Jeez, let's see... What's that?

12:52.897 --> 12:56.317
Hey, old hag.
What's inside this wicker trunk?

12:56.400 --> 13:00.988
I don't know. The unpacked ones are
exactly the same as when I bought them.

13:01.614 --> 13:03.324
You're such a slob.

13:07.161 --> 13:08.579
Mr. Maki!

13:08.662 --> 13:11.290
Good timing!
Some people are looking for you--

13:11.373 --> 13:12.792
Natsuki!

13:12.875 --> 13:15.711
You little shit!
There you go slacking off again!

13:16.587 --> 13:17.546
I'm sorry.

13:18.923 --> 13:21.926
Hey, Natsuki.
Things are about to get busy.

13:22.009 --> 13:23.427
This stuff!

13:23.511 --> 13:26.597
We're gonna sell it off here in Mastema.

13:28.015 --> 13:30.810
Black powder? Where did you get so much?

13:32.102 --> 13:34.313
The grains are rough, Mr. Maki.

13:34.396 --> 13:37.817
Aren't you the sharp one?
This powder's all fake.

13:38.692 --> 13:43.113
It's been years since our boss left,
so the real stuff has finally run out.

13:43.197 --> 13:47.368
The guys around here are so dumb,
they'll pay a fortune for it.

13:47.451 --> 13:48.828
No way.

13:48.911 --> 13:52.623
The Cross-Eyes use the black powder
to help those without magic.

13:53.207 --> 13:58.003
Most people became Cross-Eyes for money.
Wasn't that the same for you?

13:58.087 --> 14:01.507
No, it wasn't!
I don't care about the money at all.

14:01.590 --> 14:03.759
I'm not helping with that.

14:05.094 --> 14:09.890
You bastard! After all the kindness
I showed you up to now! Natsuki!

14:10.683 --> 14:12.893
Well, well, what's going on here?

14:12.977 --> 14:14.979
Trouble among friends?

14:15.479 --> 14:19.149
Who the hell are you?
Never seen your face before.

14:19.233 --> 14:23.654
Now, who could I be?
Well, even I don't really know myself.

14:23.737 --> 14:27.283
Don't tell me you're one of Dokuga's men.

14:27.366 --> 14:29.869
You trying to mess with my business--

14:30.494 --> 14:31.662
What?

14:34.123 --> 14:36.125
Natsuki!

14:36.709 --> 14:38.043
You piece of shit!

14:39.044 --> 14:40.045
I'm gonna kill you!

14:44.049 --> 14:45.259
You damn punk!

15:01.817 --> 15:03.027
Mr. Maki.

15:03.110 --> 15:05.029
I feel sorry for you.

15:05.112 --> 15:09.533
I heard that real Cross-Eyes members
are incredible with knives.

15:10.492 --> 15:12.578
You're strong, so you're the real deal?

15:12.661 --> 15:14.163
I don't know.

15:14.246 --> 15:17.416
Just go home already.
And quit the Cross-Eyes.

15:17.499 --> 15:20.794
No way. I've decided to stick with you!

15:20.878 --> 15:22.504
Then I'll meet the boss one day!

15:22.588 --> 15:25.174
Not happening! You're a total pain!

15:25.257 --> 15:28.844
I'm begging you, please!
I'll do whatever you say!

15:28.928 --> 15:34.183
Hey, Nikaido, you give her a firm no! Hey!

15:34.266 --> 15:38.062
Hand over the money, you damn scum!

15:47.863 --> 15:49.698
Dokuga. It's over there.

15:55.037 --> 15:55.955
It's Kento.

15:56.664 --> 15:59.458
He used magic
from the smoke shop to gigantify.

15:59.541 --> 16:02.544
Dokuga! This is bad.
Everyone's been killed.

16:07.383 --> 16:09.843
This is En's cleaner car.

16:10.886 --> 16:13.097
They took out Kento and the others.

16:13.180 --> 16:15.599
Dammit! What the hell's going on?

16:15.683 --> 16:18.185
To think everything would turn to ashes.

16:19.937 --> 16:22.314
I came here
because you said there'd be food,

16:22.398 --> 16:24.733
but all you got is cold rice!

16:24.817 --> 16:28.612
Come on, it's okay.
Nikaido's cooking for you.

16:28.696 --> 16:31.740
By the way, how do we get to Berith?

16:31.824 --> 16:33.909
Maybe we should take a bus.

16:33.993 --> 16:37.121
We could ride to Zagan City
and decide then.

16:37.955 --> 16:40.457
- Zagan City?
- It's ready!

16:41.208 --> 16:44.128
Omelet rice with hardly any filling.

16:45.337 --> 16:47.631
Hardly any filling, cool!

16:47.715 --> 16:50.467
How come you're totally broke, Big Bro?

16:50.551 --> 16:52.136
I'm not your Big Bro!

16:52.720 --> 16:55.055
Hey, can I use your bathroom?

16:55.139 --> 16:56.640
Sure, over there.

16:59.101 --> 17:00.144
Hey, Big Bro.

17:00.227 --> 17:04.314
Is Nikaido your partner? Or girlfriend?

17:04.898 --> 17:08.277
Well... she's my partner.

17:09.778 --> 17:11.572
But she's not with the Cross-Eyes?

17:12.573 --> 17:16.076
The scar on my back from the church
is completely gone.

17:16.660 --> 17:18.996
Did Asu heal it for me?

17:19.663 --> 17:21.081
Well, either way,

17:21.915 --> 17:25.169
who in the world was it that stabbed me?

17:28.172 --> 17:29.590
I almost forgot.

17:29.673 --> 17:32.217
I'll leave this with you, Big Bro.

17:32.301 --> 17:33.260
What's that?

17:33.343 --> 17:35.929
Black powder, obviously.

17:36.013 --> 17:39.099
It's genuine, of course.
It's the very last bag.

17:39.183 --> 17:43.103
If you take this, even someone like me,
who can't produce smoke,

17:43.187 --> 17:46.106
can become a full-fledged Sorcerer.

17:46.190 --> 17:49.693
The boss who invented this stuff
really is something.

17:50.319 --> 17:54.531
It's done! Our grand mansion is complete!

17:54.615 --> 17:55.491
Hey!

17:55.574 --> 17:59.328
Cow, Pig! Stop messing
with the merch for our side job!

17:59.411 --> 18:01.163
What if we can't sell it?

18:01.246 --> 18:05.918
Come on. This house is built
from the envelopes we sweated over making.

18:06.001 --> 18:07.628
It has a dreamlike charm.

18:07.711 --> 18:12.132
This here is the kitchen.
And the bathroom is huge, like a spa.

18:12.216 --> 18:17.096
We've got three sinks and three toilets,
so no more need to fight in the mornings.

18:17.179 --> 18:20.641
I see. You've finally started
running from reality.

18:21.141 --> 18:23.644
By the way, Dokuga and Tetsujo are late.

18:23.727 --> 18:26.855
Isn't you-know-who
gonna be here any minute?

18:30.734 --> 18:33.278
Hello there.

18:34.696 --> 18:38.784
Hello, madam landlady.
You're looking as beautiful as ever today.

18:38.867 --> 18:43.747
Oh my, hearing that from you,
sweet handsome Saji, makes me happy.

18:45.624 --> 18:47.292
Let's get straight to it.

18:47.376 --> 18:52.297
I need you to finally pay
all six months of back rent today.

18:52.381 --> 18:57.678
I do like you guys, really.
But today's the day you pay what is owed.

18:57.761 --> 19:03.433
Dokuga will be bringing the money soon.
Ushishimada will entertain you until then.

19:03.517 --> 19:07.980
Oh my! How can I say no
to a wonderful offer like that?

19:09.773 --> 19:12.860
It's a pleasure to see you, Ushishimada.

19:12.943 --> 19:15.320
Same here, madam.

19:15.404 --> 19:17.447
Don't call me madam!

19:17.531 --> 19:19.658
I'm still single, you know!

19:20.159 --> 19:21.702
A visitor? All right!

19:21.785 --> 19:24.538
Like I've been saying,

19:24.621 --> 19:28.709
you won't have to pay rent
if you become my partner.

19:29.376 --> 19:33.881
And as for your friends,
I'll take care of them too.

19:35.716 --> 19:38.552
Dokuga should be back soon.

19:38.635 --> 19:40.888
Look! It's Dokuga and Tetsujo!

19:40.971 --> 19:42.848
What? They're back?

19:43.473 --> 19:46.935
Dokuga! We've been waiting!
What about the money?

19:50.397 --> 19:53.066
En's cleaners wiped out
Kento and the others.

19:53.150 --> 19:57.196
The last black powder
and the expensive smoke burned to ashes.

19:57.279 --> 20:03.493
What the hell! So all we've got left
are the envelopes for our side job?

20:04.286 --> 20:07.206
Do we have to leave this place too?

20:07.289 --> 20:10.334
That aside, what's Risu doing?

20:11.919 --> 20:15.088
Damn it, there's gotta be something.

20:15.172 --> 20:18.091
Some clue about the one who killed me.

20:18.717 --> 20:21.345
You trying to steal something
from my desk?

20:21.929 --> 20:25.849
Well, bad news for you.
There's nothing of monetary value here.

20:25.933 --> 20:28.477
I'm here because you keep playing dumb!

20:28.560 --> 20:31.355
Who the hell killed me?
Did the boss order it?

20:32.356 --> 20:33.774
Or maybe...

20:34.524 --> 20:36.944
It was you, Dokuga?

20:39.321 --> 20:43.742
There was a thief
who once broke into this house.

20:44.493 --> 20:49.039
Let me show you what happened to him.

20:49.915 --> 20:52.417
Either way, we're out of money.

20:52.501 --> 20:56.672
We have no choice but to leave this place
and go our separate ways.

20:56.755 --> 21:01.885
Damn it! Weren't the five of us supposed
to wait together for the boss to return?

21:01.969 --> 21:04.554
We lost to poverty.

21:05.055 --> 21:06.598
Leave it to me.

21:06.682 --> 21:07.641
- What?
- What?

21:07.724 --> 21:10.602
I'll go see the landlady.

21:11.103 --> 21:14.648
If I do that,
you'll be allowed to stay in this house.

21:14.731 --> 21:17.484
You idiot!
This is just like selling yourself.

21:17.567 --> 21:18.610
I'm a man, dammit!

21:19.528 --> 21:22.823
If this body can be of any use to you,

21:23.365 --> 21:25.492
then I'll gladly sacrifice myself.

21:26.285 --> 21:27.911
Ushishimada.

21:28.662 --> 21:30.247
You're so selfless.

21:30.330 --> 21:33.250
What are you doing? Got the money?

21:34.960 --> 21:37.796
Madam landlady, I'm sorry,
but we don't have the money.

21:38.297 --> 21:40.257
So I'll go with you instead.

21:40.340 --> 21:41.633
Oh my!

21:56.898 --> 21:59.192
What did you do to my eyes?

22:01.611 --> 22:03.196
My saliva is poisonous.

22:03.280 --> 22:04.239
Damn it!

22:16.918 --> 22:20.339
I won't kill you.
Because you're too "dangerous."

22:24.593 --> 22:27.262
This is the deed to the house.

22:27.346 --> 22:30.474
From now on,
this building belongs to you all.

22:30.557 --> 22:34.061
Well then, shall we go, Ushishimada?

22:35.354 --> 22:40.275
I really wanted to live with you guys
in that house we made out of envelopes.

22:40.359 --> 22:41.902
Farewell.

22:41.985 --> 22:44.404
- Ushishimada!
- Ushishimada!

22:54.831 --> 22:55.832
Oops.

22:57.167 --> 22:58.835
EAST BERITH

23:04.800 --> 23:06.343
Zagan.

23:06.426 --> 23:08.929
I've heard that name before.

23:09.429 --> 23:12.224
Where did I hear it?

23:12.307 --> 23:13.141
ZAGAN MAGIC TRAINING

23:17.479 --> 23:18.855
Professor Kasukabe.

23:19.356 --> 23:22.025
I became a Sorcerer.

23:22.943 --> 23:25.362
- Mr. Kasukabe.
- What?

23:25.445 --> 23:29.866
What's wrong? You're spacing out.
Are you still in pain somewhere?

23:29.950 --> 23:32.828
No, I'm fine.

23:32.911 --> 23:35.372
- That wax figure...
- A wax figure?

23:35.455 --> 23:42.003
Yeah. There was something like an altar,
and in the center, there was a wax figure.

23:42.587 --> 23:44.965
It melted in the fire, though.

23:45.966 --> 23:50.846
By the way, are those guys with crosses
on their eyes some kind of organization?

23:50.929 --> 23:54.516
They're our enemies.
We took out quite a few of them, though.

23:54.599 --> 23:57.519
Caiman has those cross marks too.

23:57.602 --> 23:59.229
Yeah, that's right!

24:00.814 --> 24:04.734
That's also important,
but that face of the figure...

24:05.610 --> 24:07.404
I know him.

24:07.487 --> 24:08.405
- What?
- What?

24:09.656 --> 24:12.242
Let's go back to the Hole.

